# Search checklist — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

<!-- init: used by search-discovery when enabled; in config.language. AEO and GEO are lenses of one
     role (D7); /hrd evolve may propose splitting them when evidence accumulates. -->

## SEO
- [ ] Title carries the primary keyword naturally and stays within {{TITLE_MAX_CHARS}} characters.
- [ ] Meta description states the answer or benefit and carries the primary keyword.
- [ ] One H1; H2/H3 headings map to sub-intents and secondary keywords.
- [ ] Slug reflects the intent (lowercase, single hyphens, no `--`).
- [ ] Internal links to related articles; no orphan article.
- [ ] Images have descriptive alt text.
- [ ] No overlap of intent with an existing article (cannibalization).

## AEO (answer engines)
- [ ] The core question is answered directly in the first paragraph.
- [ ] Question-shaped headings, each followed by a concise answer.
- [ ] Lists or tables where the answer is a set of steps, options or a comparison.
- [ ] A short FAQ when real question variants exist.

## GEO (generative engines)
- [ ] Self-contained, quotable statements with concrete numbers and named sources.
- [ ] Entities (products, organizations, places) named explicitly, not by pronoun.
- [ ] A summary that can be cited without the rest of the page.
- [ ] Freshness signals where facts change (date of the information).

